Kind: ablation
Issue: #710
Over: 710-widen-futex-early.patch
Takes out: 3cfdd44c -- i386's kernel_trap() hands a fault on a task's memory taken in the kernel to vm_fault() again whatever the thread's state, so the futex waiter that the widen held before splsched, its page unmapped by pthread_test's last case while it was held, faults on its second read with its wait declared, and vm_fault() takes the map's mutex there, which a kernel built with MACH_ASSERT refuses in mutex_lock_assert_safe(); every boot must stop there
Run: i386 -- scripts/suite-i386.sh -r bundle-kvm-4
Expect: mutex_lock_assert_safe: thread 0x[0-9a-f]+ takes a mutex with wait_event
Expect: assert_wait: already asserted event

